# =============================================================================
# Kade environment contract
# =============================================================================
# Copy to `apps/web/.env.local`, NOT to the repository root: Next.js loads env
# files from its own project directory (`apps/web`), so a root `.env.local` is
# silently ignored by the app. Scripts that read the environment (for example
# the EAS tooling in packages/contracts) take it from the shell instead.
#
# `.env*` is git-ignored except this file.
#
# Nothing here is a real secret. Never commit a filled-in copy
# (docs/week-1-frozen-delivery-contract.md section 8: secrets handling).
#
# Sources for every variable:
#   - docs/week-1-frozen-delivery-contract.md section 2.1 (fee mode), section 5
#     (day-1 dependencies), section 7 (gates)
#   - docs/planning/kade-mvp-build-document-v7.docx section 8 (architecture),
#     section 9 (schema)
#   - docs/architecture/adr/ (decisions recorded during this iteration)
# =============================================================================

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Runtime mode
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Which chain set the application treats as active.
#   testnet | mainnet
# Iteration 1 is all-testnet (week-1 contract section 2, item 7).
# Read by apps/web/src/lib/env.ts (readChainEnv) and resolved against the chain
# registry in @kade/shared. Server-side only; the browser cannot override it.
# [documented] KADE_CHAIN_ENV
KADE_CHAIN_ENV=testnet

# Which fee schedule row set is authoritative.
#   demo | production
# Amounts live in the `fee_schedule` table and are never hard-coded in the
# client (week-1 contract section 2.1).
# Read by apps/web/src/lib/env.ts (readFeeMode). Server-side only.
# [documented] KADE_FEE_MODE
KADE_FEE_MODE=demo

# Public origin of the web app. Must match the approved Google OAuth redirect
# origin exactly (week-1 contract section 5).
# [documented]
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=http://localhost:3000

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Supabase  (week-1 contract section 5: "a Supabase project and service config")
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=

# Direct Postgres connection, used only by migrations and seeds. Never shipped
# to the browser.
# [documented] week-1 contract section 5
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://postgres:postgres@127.0.0.1:54322/postgres

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Authentication
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Google OAuth and email magic link through Supabase are the permitted logins
# (week-1 contract section 2, item 2, as amended v1.2). Password authentication
# and wallet login are excluded. The provider client id/secret and the SMTP
# sender are configured in the Supabase dashboard, not here; only the callback
# path is supplied to the app.
# [documented] week-1 contract sections 2 and 5
# [arbitrary] the callback path, which follows the Supabase SSR convention.
NEXT_PUBLIC_AUTH_CALLBACK_PATH=/auth/callback

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Fee payment treasuries  (week-1 contract section 8.9 / v1.9; week-2 section 5)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Sepolia treasury address that receives the pre-approval fee. Server-only and
# deliberately not NEXT_PUBLIC_: the resident is told where to send, but the
# recipient is resolved on the server and passed to the payment screen as a
# value, so the browser cannot substitute its own address. When absent the
# payment screen reports "not configured" rather than pointing anywhere.
# [documented] supplied by the project (v1.9, section 5).
TREASURY_ADDRESS=

# Ethereum mainnet treasury address that receives USDC fees (iteration 2).
# Server-only and deliberately not NEXT_PUBLIC_, for the same reason as
# TREASURY_ADDRESS: the recipient is resolved on the server, never in the
# browser. It is read as MAINNET_TREASURY_ADDRESS by
# apps/web/src/lib/env.ts (readMainnetTreasuryAddress) and assembled for server
# use by apps/web/src/lib/config/mainnet.ts.
# When it is absent, the mainnet path disables itself and reports "not
# configured"; a value is never invented. The Week 2 freeze checklist records
# that mainnet funding/treasury is NOT supplied yet (see
# docs/planning/week-2-todo-00-config.md).
# [documented] supplied by the project (week-2 contract section 5).
MAINNET_TREASURY_ADDRESS=

# Reown/WalletConnect project id for the browser wallet modal (an injected
# browser wallet or WalletConnect). Public by nature and not a secret; when
# absent the wallet connection is disabled and the fee step reports "not
# configured" instead of throwing.
# [documented] supplied by the project (v1.9, section 5).
NEXT_PUBLIC_WALLETCONNECT_PROJECT_ID=

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Chains and RPC
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Chain ids are frozen: 1 / 11155111, 42161 / 421614, 8453 / 84532.
# (week-1 contract section 3 EXE-002; DOCX section 9 `chains` table.)
# Server-side only: none of these is NEXT_PUBLIC_, so the browser cannot read an
# endpoint carrying a provider key.
# [documented] chain ids. [arbitrary] the specific provider URLs.
SEPOLIA_RPC_URL=
ARBITRUM_SEPOLIA_RPC_URL=
BASE_SEPOLIA_RPC_URL=

# Ethereum mainnet JSON-RPC endpoint. Iteration 2 activates Ethereum mainnet
# (week-2 contract section 2.2 item 1); read by apps/web/src/lib/env.ts
# (readEthereumRpcUrl) and consumed by apps/web/src/lib/config/mainnet.ts.
# When absent the mainnet path disables itself; no endpoint is fabricated.
# [documented] supplied by the project (week-2 contract section 5).
ETHEREUM_RPC_URL=

# Reserved: Arbitrum and Base remain deferred for iteration 2 (week-2 contract
# section 2.2 item 1), so these stay empty.
ARBITRUM_RPC_URL=
BASE_RPC_URL=

# Base URL of the Bitcoin balance provider (mempool.space, Esplora-compatible).
# Optional; defaults to https://mempool.space. Server-side only: the browser
# never calls the provider, the balance is read in a server action. There is no
# API key, but the override lets a self-hosted instance be used.
# Read by apps/web/src/lib/env.ts (readBitcoinApiBase).
# [arbitrary] the provider endpoint.
KADE_BITCOIN_API_BASE=

# Optional base URL override for the EVM balance provider (Blockscout v2 REST).
# When set, every chain is read from this self-hosted explorer instead of the
# per-chain public defaults in apps/web/src/lib/wealth/evm.ts (EVM_READ_CHAINS).
# Empty uses the per-chain defaults. Server-side only: the browser never calls
# the provider. There is no API key.
# Read by apps/web/src/lib/env.ts (readEvmExplorerApiBase).
# [arbitrary] the provider endpoint.
KADE_EVM_EXPLORER_API_BASE=

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Deployment and on-chain write authority
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Server-side only: never expose these to the browser. Never commit a funded key
# (week-1 contract section 8).
#
# The Sepolia deployment payer is supplied by the project. Named for the chain
# because apps/web/src/lib/safe/deploy.ts reads SEPOLIA_DEPLOYER_PRIVATE_KEY; if
# a local `.env.local` still spells it DEPLOYER_PRIVATE_KEY, rename it there or
# the Safe deployment engine reports `not-configured`.
# [documented] week-1 contract section 5
SEPOLIA_DEPLOYER_PRIVATE_KEY=

# Authorised Sepolia EAS registration account (week-1 contract section 5).
# EAS registration is irreversible. The Onchain gate approved the encodings on
# 18 September 2026 (week-1 contract section 7, checkpoint 3) and the owner
# executed them by hand; the UIDs are recorded in
# packages/contracts/eas/registered-uids.json. The EAS tooling here has no
# broadcast mode and never reads this key.
# [documented]
EAS_REGISTRAR_PRIVATE_KEY=

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Safe deployment inputs
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Frozen in week-1 contract section 4 (D4). Changing any of these changes the
# predicted address, so they are change-control items (section 8).
#
# The Safe version is decided (v1.5.0, contract v1.6) and recorded in
# @kade/shared; the salt nonce strategy is proposed but not yet approved. The
# application reads these from @kade/shared, so the values here are overrides
# for tooling rather than the source of truth.
SAFE_VERSION=
SAFE_SALT_NONCE=
SAFE_PROXY_FACTORY_ADDRESS=
SAFE_SINGLETON_ADDRESS=
SAFE_COMPATIBILITY_FALLBACK_HANDLER_ADDRESS=
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Contracts
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Addresses are seeded into the `chains` table by migration, not read from env
# at runtime (week-1 contract section 3 EXE-002).
# [arbitrary] placeholder values.
EAS_CONTRACT_ADDRESS_SEPOLIA=0xC2679fBD37d54388Ce493F1DB75320D236e1815e
KADELOCK_ADDRESS_SEPOLIA=

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Paymaster
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Beyond what is strictly required to deploy the Week 1 Safe, paymaster policy
# is out of scope (week-1 contract section 9).
# [arbitrary]
PIMLICO_API_KEY=
PIMLICO_POLICY_ID=

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Invest — MetaMorpho vault (Week 2, D18 / EXE-014)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# One MetaMorpho vault on Ethereum mainnet (week-2 contract section 2.2 and
# 6.3). The owner clarified the Invest target is a MetaMorpho vault, not a
# Morpho Blue market: a single ERC-4626 contract with one underlying asset
# (USDC). The vault address and its underlying USDC are project-supplied and are
# NOT present yet (contract section 5, freeze checklist), so these are empty: no
# address is invented, and the Invest screen reports "vault not configured".
#
# Server-only: read by apps/web/src/lib/invest/morpho-config.ts and passed to the
# Invest screen as values, so the browser neither reads nor hard-codes them. The
# chain id is not a key here — it is CHAIN_IDS.ethereum from @kade/shared.
# [arbitrary] key names until the project confirms the vault.
KADE_MORPHO_VAULT_ADDRESS=
KADE_MORPHO_USDC_ADDRESS=
